       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily, with a note to give it with meals.\n\nThis dose adds up to 2,550 mg/day. That is the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, so it's within the limit but leaves no room to go higher. Check that the patient is on the immediate-release form and not extended-release. Before the order goes through, confirm that this is the intended dose. Patients usually start lower and increase the dose slowly, and a high dose raises the risk of GI side effects.\n\nAlso keep an eye on renal function (eGFR). You should hold metformin around iodinated contrast and for acute illness that could cause kidney injury or hypoperfusion."
